Exactly. And if you’re going to spend the time and energy anyway, why not make the experience something worth enjoying?

Same place. Same circumstances. Same obligations. But an entirely different experience depending on how you choose to engage with them.

And there’s something deeper there: fun isn’t necessarily the reward for finishing something. It can be the way you do it.

Playfulness can turn work into craftsmanship, difficulty into a challenge, and ordinary moments into memories.

You don’t always get to choose the game you’re in. But you often get to choose how you play.

And sometimes having fun is how you discover you weren’t nearly as trapped as you thought. ;)